  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lanthanide ion with no unpaired electron is diamagnetic in nature.</p><p>Lanthanoid is also called lanthanide, which can be defined as any of the series of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> consecutive chemical elements in the periodic table from lanthanum to lutetium (atomic numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>57</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>71</mn></math>). With the elements scandium and yttrium, they make up the rare-earth metals. Lanthanides are also radioactive in nature.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ce</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> diamagnetic</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>La</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>La</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> diamagnetic</p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
